---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: no memory-backed filesystem is available to stage plaintext on; nothing ran.

A generator's inputs and outputs are files, and safix places them in a
private directory on tmpfs so that no plaintext reaches a block device.
Tried:
  - /dev/shm
  - /run/user/1000
Of those, disk-backed:
  - /dev/shm

Re-run with --allow-disk-staging to accept that plaintext will be
written to a disk-backed filesystem, where an unlink leaves the bytes
in free blocks. Set SAFIX_STAGING_DIR to name a tmpfs mount instead.
